{
  "id": "ponzo-illusion",
  "term": "Ponzo illusion",
  "definition": "The Ponzo illusion is a visual illusion used to study how ambiguous retinal input is interpreted through visual context and higher-level knowledge or beliefs. It affects perceived size or magnitude and is described here as being especially influenced by top-down control from higher brain areas.",
